From 7130ba48ca7e9114e667c246c01c641bf2dbdd8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukin <mylukin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Mar 2026 16:25:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 26/98] fix: survive streaming_mode 10-min auto-close with
 proactive renewal timer and card.update fallback
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Feishu auto-closes streaming_mode 10 minutes after activation. Previously,
renewal only fired inside updateCardContent(), so long-running LLM thinking
phases with no output left streaming_mode to expire silently. On close(),
the final content update via cardElement.content() would fail while the
summary via card.settings() still succeeded — producing cards with stale
body text but correct summaries.

Two-layer fix:
- Proactive setInterval timer renews streaming_mode every 8 minutes
  independently of content updates, keeping the session alive during
  idle periods. Timer is unref()'d to not block process shutdown.
- Fallback in close(): if the streaming element API fails, fall back to
  card.update() which works regardless of streaming_mode state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
